   - $\text{BRR} = 1476$ ($0\times 05\text{C4}$) sets the baud rate to $115{,}200$ baud with an insignificant error of $-0.021\,\%$.
   - The baud-rate register is written prior to setting `UE` in `CR1`. Setting `TE`, `RE`, and `UE` simultaneously configures an 8-bit, no-parity, 1-stop-bit bidirectional serial link.

