- **Target PWM Frequency:** $f_\text{PWM} = 1000\text{ Hz}$ (1 kHz)
- **Target Duty Cycle:** $50\%$

Using standard up-counting edge-aligned PWM Mode 1:
$$f_\text{PWM} = \frac{f_\text{TIM}}{(\text{PSC} + 1) \times (\text{ARR} + 1)}$$

With:
- **$\text{PSC} = 3$** (prescaler division ratio $\text{PSC} + 1 = 4$)
- **$\text{ARR} = 42499$** ($\text{ARR} + 1 = 42500$ counts)
  $$\frac{170\,000\,000}{(3 + 1) \times (42499 + 1)} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{170\,000} = 1000\text{ Hz} \quad (0.0\%\text{ frequency error})$$
- **$\text{CCR1} = 21250$**:
  $$\text{Duty} = \frac{\text{CCR1}}{\text{ARR} + 1} = \frac{21\,250}{42\,500} = 50.0\% \quad (0.0\%\text{ duty error})$$

