### Pin Allocation Conflict and Resolution

On the STM32G474, hardware signals for USART1 (`USART1_TX` and `USART1_RX`) do not exist on pins PA2 and PA3 [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73]:
- **PA2** supports alternate functions: TIM2_CH3 (AF1), TIM5_CH3 (AF2), USART2_TX (AF7), COMP2_OUT (AF8), TIM15_CH1 (AF9), QUADSPI1_BK1_NCS (AF10), and LPUART1_TX (AF12) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73].
- **PA3** supports alternate functions: TIM2_CH4 (AF1), TIM5_CH4 (AF2), SAI1_CK1 (AF3), USART2_RX (AF7), TIM15_CH2 (AF9), QUADSPI1_CLK (AF10), and LPUART1_RX (AF12) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73].
- The available alternate function pins for USART1 on STM32G474 are:
  - `USART1_TX`: **PA9** (AF7), **PB6** (AF7), **PC4** (AF7) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73, p.74, p.75].
  - `USART1_RX`: **PA10** (AF7), **PB7** (AF7), **PC5** (AF7) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73, p.74, p.75].

Because you specified that USART2 is dedicated to an RS-485 transceiver and this console must use USART1, the configuration is mapped to the standard USART1 pin pair:
- **TX:** **PA9** (Alternate Function 7)
- **RX:** **PA10** (Alternate Function 7)

*(Note: If board routing strictly requires physical pins PA2/PA3 without altering the USART2 RS-485 transceiver assignment, LPUART1 on PA2/PA3 at AF12 can be used as an alternative).*

---

### Clock and Baud Rate Calculation

- **Peripheral Clock:** By default, USART1 clock selection (`RCC->CCIPR`, `USART1SEL[1:0] = 00b`) selects **PCLK2** [STM32G474_RM0440 p.322].
- Clock frequency: $f_{\text{PCLK2}} = 170\,000\,000\text{ Hz}$.
- Oversampling by 16 (`OVER8 = 0` in `USART_CR1`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1740].
- Formula [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1755]:
  $$\text{BRR} = \frac{f_{\text{CK}}}{\text{Baud}} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{115\,200} \approx 1475.69 \implies \text{BRR} = 1476 \text{ (0x000005C4)}$$
- Resulting baud rate:
  $$\text{Baud}_{\text{actual}} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{1476} \approx 115176.15\text{ baud (error: } -0.021\%\text{)}$$

---

### Bare-Metal CMSIS C Code

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void usart1_init(void) {
    /* 1. Enable GPIOA and USART1 peripheral clock gates */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN;
    RCC->APB2ENR |= RCC_APB2ENR_USART1EN;

    /* 2. Configure PA9 (TX) and PA10 (RX) in Alternate Function mode (MODER = 10b) */
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE10_Msk);
    GPIOA->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE10_Pos);

    /* Set High speed on TX pin */
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED9_Pos);

    /* Set AF7 (USART1) for PA9 and PA10 in AFRH (AFR[1]) */
    GPIOA->AFR[1] &= ~((0xFU << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos) | (0xFU << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL10_Pos));
    GPIOA->AFR[1] |= (7U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos) | (7U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL10_Pos);

    /* 3. Configure USART1: 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, oversampling by 16 */
    USART1->CR1 = 0U;  /* UE=0, M0=0 (8 data bits), PCE=0 (no parity), OVER8=0 (oversample by 16) */
    USART1->CR2 = 0U;  /* STOP=00b (1 stop bit) */
    USART1->CR3 = 0U;

    /* 4. Write Baud Rate Register before enabling USART1: 170 MHz / 115200 = 1476 */
    USART1->BRR = 1476U;

    /* 5. Enable Transmitter (TE) and Receiver (RE) */
    USART1->CR1 = USART_CR1_TE | USART_CR1_RE;

    /* 6. Enable USART1 peripheral (UE = 1) */
    USART1->CR1 |= USART_CR1_UE;
}
```

### Pin and Signal Allocation

- **Pin:** `PA6`
- **Signal:** `TIM3_CH1`
- **Alternate Function:** `AF2` [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73]
- **GPIO Mode:** Alternate function mode (`MODER[13:12] = 10b`), push-pull output.

---

### Timer Calculations (1 kHz, 50 % Duty Cycle)

- **Timer Kernel Clock ($f_{\text{TIM3CLK}}$):**
  TIM3 is on the APB1 domain. According to RM0440 §7.2.13 ("Timer clock"), when the APB prescaler equals 1, the timer clock frequencies are set to the same frequency as the APB domain [STM32G474_RM0440 p.281].
  With $PCLK1 = 170\text{ MHz}$ and APB1 prescaler = 1:
  $$f_{\text{TIM3CLK}} = 170\,000\,000\text{ Hz}$$

- **PWM Frequency (1 kHz):**
  $$f_{\text{PWM}} = \frac{f_{\text{TIM3CLK}}}{(\text{PSC} + 1) \times (\text{ARR} + 1)}$$
  Selecting $\text{PSC} = 3$ gives:
  $$\text{ARR} + 1 = \frac{170\,000\,000}{(3 + 1) \times 1000} = 42\,500 \implies \text{ARR} = 42\,499 \quad (\text{0xA603})$$
  This results in exactly $1\,000\text{ Hz}$ ($0.0\%$ error) within the 16-bit counter range ($\text{ARR} \le 65535$).

- **Duty Cycle (50 %, PWM Mode 1, Active-High):**
  In edge-aligned PWM mode 1 with upcounting, the reference signal is high as long as $\text{CNT} < \text{CCR1}$ and becomes low when $\text{CNT} \ge \text{CCR1}$ [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1179]:
  $$\text{CCR1} = (\text{ARR} + 1) \times 50\% = 42\,500 \times 0.5 = 21\,250 \quad (\text{0x5302})$$

