### STM32G474 Clock Configuration for 170 MHz Operation (VDD = 3.6 V)

#### 1. Hardware Specifications & Operating Limits
- **Supply Voltage ($V_{DD}$)**: The board supply is fixed at 3.6 V, which falls within the recommended operating range of 1.71 V to 3.6 V [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84].
- **Core Voltage Regulator Mode**:
  - For system clock frequencies above 150 MHz and up to 170 MHz, the device requires **Range 1 Boost Mode** [STM32G474_RM0440 p.232].
  - In Range 1 Boost Mode, the internal regulator provides a nominal core voltage $V_{CORE} = 1.28\text{ V}$ [STM32G474_RM0440 p.232].
  - To enter Boost Mode, the `R1MODE` bit (bit 8) in the `PWR_CR5` register must be cleared (`0`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.267].
- **Flash Read Access Latency**:
  - According to the Flash latency table for Category 3 devices in Range 1 Boost Mode, HCLK frequencies up to 170 MHz require **4 wait states (5 CPU cycles)** (`LATENCY = 4`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.98].
  - Enabling the prefetch buffer (`PRFTEN`), instruction cache (`ICEN`), and data cache (`DCEN`) in `FLASH_ACR` ensures maximum execution throughput [STM32G474_RM0440 p.130].
- **PLL Parameter Limits & Clock Synthesis**:
  - Clock source: Internal 16 MHz HSI16 oscillator [STM32G474_Datasheet p.120].
  - Division factor $M$: Set to $M = 4$, yielding an input frequency $f_{\text{PLL\_IN}} = \frac{16\text{ MHz}}{4} = 4\text{ MHz}$, which satisfies the required range of 2.66 MHz to 16 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123].
  - Multiplier factor $N$: Set to $N = 85$, yielding a VCO frequency $f_{\text{VCO\_OUT}} = 4\text{ MHz} \times 85 = 340\text{ MHz}$, within the Range 1 VCO limits of 96 MHz to 344 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123].
  - Output divider $R$: Set to $R = 2$, yielding $f_{\text{PLL\_R}} = \frac{340\text{ MHz}}{2} = 170\text{ MHz}$, which matches the maximum rated SYSCLK/HCLK of 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost Mode [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84] [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123].
  - AHB Prescaler $HPRE = 1 \implies HCLK = 170\text{ MHz}$.
  - APB1 Prescaler $PPRE1 = 1 \implies PCLK1 = 170\text{ MHz}$ (maximum allowed: 170 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84]).
  - APB2 Prescaler $PPRE2 = 1 \implies PCLK2 = 170\text{ MHz}$ (maximum allowed: 170 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84]).

---

#### 2. Bare-Metal CMSIS Implementation (`system_clock_config.c`)

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

/**
 * @brief  Configures the system clock to 170 MHz on an STM32G474 (VDD = 3.6 V).
 *         Uses the internal 16 MHz HSI oscillator and the main PLL.
 */
void SystemClock_Config(void)
{
    /* 1. Enable power interface clock to access PWR registers */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;
    (void)RCC->APB1ENR1; // Read-after-write delay to guarantee clock enable

    /* 2. Configure Main Regulator in Range 1 Boost Mode (SYSCLK > 150 MHz up to 170 MHz)
     * Clear R1MODE (bit 8) in PWR_CR5 to select Boost Mode [STM32G474_RM0440 p.232, p.267]
     */
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    /* 3. Configure Flash latency:
     * 4 wait states (5 CPU cycles) required for 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost Mode [STM32G474_RM0440 p.98]
     * Enable prefetch, instruction cache, and data cache [STM32G474_RM0440 p.130]
     */
    FLASH->ACR = (FLASH->ACR & ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_Msk) | FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS;
    FLASH->ACR |= FLASH_ACR_PRFTEN | FLASH_ACR_ICEN | FLASH_ACR_DCEN;
    while ((FLASH->ACR & FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_Msk) != FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS);

    /* 4. Ensure HSI16 is ON and stable */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSION;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSIRDY));

    /* 5. Configure Main PLL:
     *    Source: HSI16 (16 MHz)
     *    M = /4 (field value 3)  => PLL_IN = 4 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]
     *    N = *85 (field value 85) => VCO = 340 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]
     *    R = /2 (field value 0)  => PLL_R = 170 MHz [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]
     */
    RCC->CR &= ~RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY); // Wait until PLL is disabled before reconfiguring

    RCC->PLLCFGR = RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_HSI |
                   (3U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos) |
                   (85U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos) |
                   (0U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLR_Pos) |
                   RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;

    /* Enable PLL and wait for lock */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY));

    /* 6. Switch system clock to PLL:
     * As recommended in RM0440, set intermediate AHB prescaler division (/2) before
     * switching to the higher frequency PLL clock, switch SYSCLK, then restore /1 [STM32G474_RM0440 p.232].
     */
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_HPRE_Msk) | RCC_CFGR_HPRE_DIV2;

    /* Select PLL as SYSCLK source */
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_SW_Msk) | RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS_Msk) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL);

    /* Brief wait to let internal clock domain stabilize */
    for (volatile int i = 0; i < 200; i++);

    /* Restore AHB prescaler to /1 (HCLK = 170 MHz) */
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_HPRE_Msk) | RCC_CFGR_HPRE_DIV1;
}
