  - Recommended operating voltage range for $V_{DD}$: **1.71 V to 3.6 V** [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84, Table 17]. 3.6 V is right at the maximum recommended limit.
  - Absolute maximum rating for $V_{DD} - V_{SS}$: **-0.3 V to 4.0 V** [STM32G474_Datasheet p.82, Table 14]. Operation at 3.6 V is safely below the 4.0 V absolute maximum rating.
  - The internal linear voltage regulator supplies $V_{CORE}$ for the digital core [STM32G474_Datasheet p.24].

#### 2. Clock Tree & Performance Requirements for 170 MHz
- **Voltage Scaling (Range 1 Boost Mode)**:
  - To operate at frequencies up to 170 MHz ($SYSCLK > 150\text{ MHz}$), the core regulator must run in **Range 1 Boost Mode** ($V_{CORE} \approx 1.28\text{ V}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.232, Section 6.1.5; Table 38 p.233].
  - Range 1 Boost mode is enabled by clearing the `R1MODE` bit (bit 8) in the `PWR_CR5` register (`0: Main regulator in range 1 boost mode`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.267].
  - Writing to `PWR_CR5` requires enabling the `PWR` peripheral clock gate in `RCC->APB1ENR1` (`RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN`, bit 28) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.309].
- **Flash Access Latency (Wait States)**:
  - In Range 1 Boost mode at $136\text{ MHz} < HCLK \le 170\text{ MHz}$, flash memory requires **4 Wait States (LATENCY = 4)** [STM32G474_RM0440 p.98, Table 9 (category 3 devices)].
- **PLL Configuration (using internal 16 MHz HSI16)**:
  - Input clock: $f_{\text{HSI16}} = 16\text{ MHz}$
  - Division factor $M = 4 \implies f_{\text{PLL\_IN}} = 16\text{ MHz} / 4 = 4.0\text{ MHz}$ (compliant with recommended PLL input range of $2.66\text{ MHz} - 16\text{ MHz}$) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123, Table 46].
  - Multiplication factor $N = 85 \implies f_{\text{VCO}} = 4.0\text{ MHz} \times 85 = 340.0\text{ MHz}$ (compliant with VCO output range of $96\text{ MHz} - 344\text{ MHz}$ in Range 1) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123, Table 46].
  - Division factor $R = 2 \implies f_{\text{PLL\_R}} = 340.0\text{ MHz} / 2 = 170.0\text{ MHz}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123, Table 46].
  - PLL R output enabled via `PLLREN` bit [STM32G474_RM0440 p.291].
  - AHB Prescaler: $/1$ ($HCLK = 170\text{ MHz}$), APB1 Prescaler: $/1$ ($PCLK1 = 170\text{ MHz}$), APB2 Prescaler: $/1$ ($PCLK2 = 170\text{ MHz}$).

#### 3. Bare-Metal CMSIS C Code (`rcc_config_170mhz.c`)

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void SystemClock_Config_170MHz(void)
{
    /* 1. Enable power interface clock in RCC_APB1ENR1 */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;

    /* 2. Configure Main Regulator into Range 1 Boost mode by clearing R1MODE in PWR_CR5.
     *    Required when SYSCLK > 150 MHz (up to 170 MHz).
     */
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    /* 3. Configure Flash Read Access Latency:
     *    In Range 1 Boost mode, 4 wait states (5 CPU cycles) are required for HCLK = 170 MHz.
     */
    FLASH->ACR = (FLASH->ACR & ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY) | FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS;
    while ((FLASH->ACR & FLASH_ACR_LATENCY) != FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS) {
        /* Wait for Flash latency to take effect */
    }

    /* 4. Ensure HSI16 is enabled and ready */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSION;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSIRDY)) {
        /* Wait until HSI16 is ready */
    }

    /* 5. Disable Main PLL before reconfiguring */
    RCC->CR &= ~RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY) {
        /* Wait until PLL is stopped */
    }

    /* 6. Configure Main PLL:
     *    - Source: HSI16 (16 MHz)
     *    - M = 4: f_PLL_IN = 16 MHz / 4 = 4 MHz (PLLM bits: 3 -> /4)
     *    - N = 85: f_VCO = 4 MHz * 85 = 340 MHz
     *    - R = 2: f_SYSCLK = 340 MHz / 2 = 170 MHz (PLLR bits: 0 -> /2)
     *    - Enable PLLCLK (PLL "R" output)
     */
    RCC->PLLCFGR = RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_HSI |
                   (3U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos) |
                   (85U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos) |
                   (0U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLR_Pos) |
                   RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;

    /* 7. Enable Main PLL and wait for lock */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY)) {
        /* Wait for PLL ready */
    }

    /* 8. Configure AHB, APB1, and APB2 prescalers to /1 */
    RCC->CFGR &= ~(RCC_CFGR_HPRE | RCC_CFGR_PPRE1 | RCC_CFGR_PPRE2);

    /* 9. Switch System Clock (SYSCLK) to PLL */
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_SW) | RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL) {
        /* Wait until PLL is selected as system clock source */
    }
}
```

